A||N||7||kornholio||removing catalytic convertor||||5
Z||000000||kornholio||09-18-1999||05:27 PM||||What does removing it actually do?  The previous owner replaced it with a straight pipe.  If I put one back in, would it make my Fiero run quieter at all?  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||09-18-1999||06:53 PM||||The cat cleans up the exhaust for emission control. Yes, a cat will quiet down the exhaust some because it create a restriction. It also slightly reduces power.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||09-18-1999||07:07 PM||||Well, if you have emissions certification in your area, you will be replacing it during your next inspection.  If not, one could convienently forget that they ever noticed it was missing, since, the difference in exhaust noise would not be enough to justify replacing it for that reason alone. However, please note that a good high flow cat like a Dynomax or Catco will not significantly degrade performance.  It may even help prevent horrible environmental catastrophies like acid rain, and ozone layer holes, which could harm the paint on your Fiero.  :-)||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||09-18-1999||10:11 PM||||I've measured the back pressure of my V6 and the cat isn't a back pressure issue if you use a good cat. It should still be under $125.<P>The stock system still doesn't exceed the 1.5PSI limit even at WOT.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-19-1999||12:16 AM||||1. Fiero exhaust is so short that a properly working catalyst is a non issue in all but racing, Track Only, applications.<P>2. Removal/alteration of emmission devices is a violation of Federal, and in most cases State laws. The fact that some states don't check well is not a good thing. Those states will likely be checking at some point..... The USEPA is really pushing this.<P>3. The OEM ECM PROM is programmed to have the catalyst present. Removing it changes the "back pressure" in the system. This can actually have a negative effect on performance. Most often it hurts you Torq number. Reducing Torq drops your performance out of the hole. Adding a couple HP, which may happen by reducing back pressure, will likely not be noticable.||||reg||2
Z||000005||yellowFormula||09-19-1999||12:50 AM||||When I first bought my car it had the catalytic convertor removed with just a straight pipe on it, and it was louder before I put a new cat on, but it wasn't THAT much louder. Plus in the state of MD you need it to pass emissions so I needed one anyway, but I have heard a lot of reasons why you should leave it on.||||reg||1
Z||000006||PaUL||09-19-1999||01:40 AM||||In my state cats are not required. I replace mine with a straight pipe years ago. I dont know about cats, seems to me that cause more emissions. Ever smell that rotten egg odor from your own exhaust or the car ahead of  you? Cars without cats dont produce that smell.||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||09-19-1999||09:28 AM||||Well technically, Ogre is right about the stupid federal mandated laws requiring cats. Some states just choose NOT to enforce them. I live in the middle of cattle grazing country where ALL the ranchers yank those suckers off, because they get super hot and start grass fires when they're driving out in the fields. Anybody tries to enforce the laws here will have a huge lynch mob after them.<P>That rotten egg smell is hydrogen sulfide and means the cat's not working right. A properly working cat actually does help control emissions and I can see that it's neccessary in large population areas, but of course the feds have to try and force the laws onto everyone...even us free spirited hotrodders out on the wide open plains in the middle of nowhere.<P>Screw 'em, throw me in jail, I don't give a guano. "Pull over, this is the cat police! You're in a heap of trouble, boy!" Well, I'm NEVER putting a cat onto my Batmobile or my street rods (which are not computer controlled cars). They can kiss my batty butt. However, these cars are not everyday drivers. I leave the cat on my commuter car, that's good enough for me. A poor attitude for an environmental scientist, huh. Ok, I'll step down off my soap box now.||||reg||1
